; status: works — `toward .p` only picks the SIDE, not a point on the bisector.
; .int is the constructed point (1/4, 0); it sits in the lower-left sector, so it
; selects the a–c diagonal — which does NOT pass through .int. Any point in that
; sector would give the same crease.
paper square
--v: fold .a to .b      ; vertical midline x = 1/2
--h: fold .b to .c      ; horizontal midline y = 1/2

--left: through .a .d
--bottom: through .a .b
--quartered: bisect --v --left
.int: cross --quartered --bottom

bisect --v --h toward .int
